      {
        "id": 219868,
        "name": "FrivYeti",
        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-20T16:22:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Second, KNYFE-Haka somehow makes me sad for Haka. Like, KNYFE would be a love-'em-and-leave-'em type, and Haka has such a kindhearted yet fundamentally lonely existence, I don't want to do that to him. Or think that he'd fall for it. So did he get with KNYFE out of some kind of pity? Was it a lapse? Was it something that he put a lot of thought into, and did it turn into a much longer relationship than Paige expected? Augh, this one bothers me! I just can't see Haka getting thrown by the wayside.</p>\n<p><em>goes back to listen to the Haka episode, when I asked about Haka and KNYFE getting into a bar brawl</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I actually think it really works. Haka is someone that we've established is both kindhearted and doesn't get really close to people, because he's lived so long and feels it. I think he is someone that would be totally into some no-strings-attached times with KNYFE, which will be awesome when it happens and not include any long-term commitments. In fact, I sort of think that explicitly no-strings-attached is how Haka would prefer his relationships these days; he doesn't want to get too attached, and he's much too kind to start a relationship with someone that they would expect to be long-lasting.</p>",
