      {
        "id": 219870,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-21T16:12:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"FrivYeti\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/48/1919_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> FrivYeti:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In fact, I sort of think that explicitly no-strings-attached is how Haka would prefer his relationships these days; he doesn’t want to get too attached, and he’s much too kind to start a relationship with someone that they would expect to be long-lasting.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>But it certainly would be long-lasting TO THEM, so Haka wouldn’t be sparing them something difficult out of kindness to them. He’d be doing it for himself. I’m not saying he’s so selfless that he doesn’t think about his own well-being at all, just that I don’t see any reason why he’d shy away from relationships. I don’t see him as a one-night stand kind of person.</p>\n<p>By the way, I could see that story about Haka showing up at the death of his son reaching opening-sequence-of-Up levels of feels.</p>\n<p>Maybe - and I think I’m probably reaching here, but it would be fun - Haka/KNYFE lasted a little while?</p>\n<p>Or, because it’s Christopher, Adam, and Haka, it was probably right at the end of the Multiverse and he gets sucked into the Miststorm universe and we’ll never know.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:52:15.882Z",
