      {
        "id": 263959,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-06T16:21:04.328Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Haven’t listened to the episode yet, but I juuuuust HAD to read the thread, and now here we are.</p>\n<p>Haka walks out of the room looking slightly embarrassed.  Someone (I’ll say Unity maybe) turns to Knyfe.  “Why did you climb the mountain?” “Because it was there.”</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\" data-post=\"33\" data-topic=\"18232\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>After the follow-up, I’ve had to rethink how I approach the RPG character I’ve referenced a few times. I could completely see fans doing a ship of this character with Lillian.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Please tell me it wasn’t Night-Mister.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Okay, now into the episode, and my thought on KNYFE: there has to have been at least one incident during her Filter days, even if she never had any control over which universe she went to, she had to have at least once seen some dude who was a famous sexy celebrity from her own universe, but in this reality he never had a career and isn’t all unattainable, so she’s just like “ah heck, when am I gonna get another crack at Schnonny Schnepp slash Schanning Shnatum slash Schmillian Schmurphy slash whoever you like”.</p>\n<p>“He’s a Baron and he has a Countess.” Well yeah, he’s European nobility, obviously he’s gonna try to marry up.  “You bring me the wealth and titles of the Country of Mittermania; I bring you a super-genius father for your potential children, and an eternally young super-human with a sweet goatee for your bedchamber.”</p>\n<p>There has to be at least one moment, during a battle with Ra and Fanatic, after they nearly die fighting a bunch of villains side to side, where they just suddenly, animalistically start pawing at each other for a minute or so, before finally Fanatic tears herself away and maybe curses at him for tempting her with his stupid sexy manflesh, and she flies away, and he grumbles about being left hanging and stalks off to find something he can set fire to.</p>\n<p>We need the restless ghost of Vincent Hargraves as a new monster for Dark Watch featuring the Wraith.  Because <em>he’s</em> a wraith now, and his name is HarGRAVES.  Badumtish.</p>",
        "post_number": 35,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-10-06T22:41:17.470Z",
